  "notes": "NOTE: Denver College of Nursing operates on a QUARTER system ('Denver College of Nursing operates on a quarter system and awards quarter credits for courses' — official admissions page). All credits below are QUARTER credits. The 7 quarters are seeded as published, with documented exclusion from the 8-12 semester-count validation rule (quarter-system program, not a semester plan). This is a DEGREE-COMPLETION program: the official BSN program page states it is 'for the student that has already met the prerequisite requirements for the BSN completion program and consists of seven quarters (21 months) of nursing courses.' Degree total = 180 quarter credits = 100 at DCN + 80 transfer quarter credits (56 semester credits) of prerequisite coursework. Applicants with a prior baccalaureate degree need 21 semester credits (32 quarter credits) of prerequisites. Course categories follow the page's own totals: Program Nursing Credits 87 (all NUR courses) and Program Gen-Ed Credits 13 (BIO309, HIT410, SOC321). A minimum of 75% of the DCN program courses must be earned at Denver College of Nursing. The BSN completion program is offered at the Denver and Houston campuses (official BSN page: 'the option to study at our Denver or Houston, Texas, campuses'; official Apply page lists 'Bachelor of Science in Nursing - Houston Campus' separately). The ADN is Denver-campus only and the RN-to-BSN and MSN are online-only; none is a Houston-campus program. Course codes are printed on the page without spaces (BIO309, NUR310, etc.) and are kept verbatim.",
